sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch11-15> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch11-15--grok> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch11-15--grok> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 on thompson1917-ch11-15: resolvable-now, resolvability 0.71" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.708"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "resolvable-now" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.7"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "Both angles are standard shell measurements, and the four body forms are common in public photograph and scan collections. The contrast he draws is quantitative and can be accepted or rejected from a modest sample of each form. Orientation error is manageable on 3D meshes and on well-posed photographs." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: For Cerithium, Solarium (Architectonica), Natica, Planorbis and similar shells, estimate the spiral angle and the apical angle of the enveloping cone. Similar spiral angles with apical angles that track the visible form difference support the claim; large spiral-angle differences among these shells refute it." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Apical angle and spiral angle can be confused on a single photograph if the axis is not in the plane of the picture.", "Modern genus limits differ from Thompson's Solarium and Planorbis, so the sample has to follow the shapes he named." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/thompson1917-ch11-15--grok--dataset-1>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/thompson1917-ch11-15--grok--dataset-2>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/thompson1917-ch11-15--grok--dataset-3> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch11-15--grok--operationalizability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Operationalizability of thompson1917-ch11-15 by Grok 4.7: 0.85" ;
